{
    "background_story": "Ivanna was a free-spirited artist known for her whimsical and often impractical ideas. Her friends and family affectionately referred to her as a 'dreamer', always chasing the next big thing. Ivanna's life was a series of follies, from attempting to start a career as a professional snail trainer to investing in a machine that turned thoughts into art. While her endeavors often ended in humorous failure, Ivanna never lost her enthusiasm. She once spent an entire summer building a giant sculpture of a rabbit out of recycled materials, only to have it collapse in a strong gust of wind. Despite the setbacks, Ivanna's creativity and infectious laughter inspired those around her. Her studio became a haven for misfits and creatives, where they could share their own tales of folly and find solace in Ivanna's unwavering optimism.",
